«
@@ ============================================================
@@ T₀SDAToB — Julian Day of closest approach between two bodies (windowed)
@@ Minimum of the inter-body distance inside [JD1,JD2], found as the root of
@@ its centred difference by bisection.
@@ Author & design         : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@
@@ Input  : 'Af' 'Bf' JD1 JD2   ( 'Af' 'Bf' JD1 JD2 -- JDmin )
@@ Output : JD of minimum distance
@@ VALIDATION (device-confirmed):
@@   'Ⓛ♁Φf' 'Ⓛ♂Φf' 2459120 2459140 T₀SDAToB -> 2459129.07   (2020-10-06)
@@
@@ Bisection rather than Root: PosΦf reaches EaΦf, which solves Kepler with
@@ Root of its own. A Root evaluated inside another Root diverges, and the
@@ outer one then returns its own lower bound as though it had converged --
@@ silently, since it believes it has a solution. Bisection needs no solver,
@@ no tolerance and no derivative: the centred difference changes sign across
@@ the minimum, which is all that is required.
@@
@@ The difference is written out at both places it is needed rather than held
@@ in a program: a program that mentions the enclosing locals resolves them by
@@ position, and the position moves as the loop pushes frames of its own.
@@ ============================================================
 → Af Bf JD1 JD2
  « JD1 →Num JD2 →Num
    JD1 →Num 0.5 + Af EVAL ⓁPosΦf  JD1 0.5 + Bf EVAL ⓁPosΦf  ⓁDAToB Uval
    JD1 →Num 0.5 - Af EVAL ⓁPosΦf  JD1 0.5 - Bf EVAL ⓁPosΦf  ⓁDAToB Uval -
    1 45 FOR i
      → lo hi flo
      « lo hi + 2 /
        → mid
        « mid 0.5 + Af EVAL ⓁPosΦf  mid 0.5 + Bf EVAL ⓁPosΦf  ⓁDAToB Uval
          mid 0.5 - Af EVAL ⓁPosΦf  mid 0.5 - Bf EVAL ⓁPosΦf  ⓁDAToB Uval -
          → fm
          « IF fm flo * 0 < THEN lo mid flo ELSE mid hi fm END »
        »
      »
    NEXT
    DROP + 2 /
  »
»
